@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Simple profile diagram — one Stereotype «Service» extending the Component metaclass with one tagged value.
'   usecase:      Teach stereotype, metaclass, extension (filled triangle arrowhead), tagged value definition, and the profile package.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       Software Architecture
' ============================================================================
title Example Profile Diagram - Simple Stereotype

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' A PROFILE is a package that defines STEREOTYPES — lightweight extensions of
' the UML metamodel.  Each stereotype EXTENDS a metaclass (e.g. Component,
' Class) and may declare TAGGED VALUES (extra attributes that can be attached
' to any model element bearing the stereotype).
'
' Strict UML uses an EXTENSION relationship with a FILLED TRIANGLE arrowhead
' pointing from the stereotype to the metaclass.  PlantUML has no native
' "extension" line, so we emulate it with a dependency arrow (..) plus a
' stereotype label and an explicit note.  This is the documented workaround.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

package "MicroserviceProfile" <<profile>> {

  ' METACLASS — a UML base type being extended.
  class Component << (M,#B4A7E5) metaclass >> {
  }

  ' STEREOTYPE — a user-defined extension providing tagged values.
  class Service << (S,#F2C9C9) stereotype >> {
    + endpoint : String
  }

  ' EXTENSION: Service extends Component.  The dashed line with a filled
  ' triangle (shown via the note) is the UML extension arrow.
  Service ..> Component : <<extend>>

  note right of Service
    <b>Stereotype</b> «Service»
    Extends metaclass Component.
    Tagged value:
      endpoint : String
    Apply as:
      «Service» (endpoint="/v1/charge")
      on any Component.
  end note
}

note bottom of Component
  <b>Reading the extension arrow</b>
  Stereotype ----triangle> Metaclass
  (filled head points to metaclass)
  means: "elements of type Component
  may optionally carry «Service» and
  its tagged values."
end note

@enduml
